   "text": {
    "L1": "Look at the first odd numbers: 1, 3, 5, and 7. Their total is a square number.",
    "L2": "Start with one dot. Add 3 dots as an L, and the dots form a 2 by 2 square.",
    "L3": "Add 5 as the next L, then 7 as the next L. The squares become 3 by 3 and then 4 by 4.",
    "L4": "So the first n odd numbers make an n by n square, because each odd number is the next L-shaped border.",
    "L5": "Do not start later or skip an odd number. For example, 3 plus 5 plus 7 plus 9 is 24, not a square.",
    "L6": "Two neighbouring triangular numbers also fit into a square: 6 and 10 fit together to make 16.",
    "L7": "Now choose the total of the first five odd numbers. Use the picture rule, not just a guess."
   },
